Static DTrace source comparison, 2026-10-13
=========================================

The combined static source inventory exceeds three times the pinned vanilla
FreeBSD inventory. Kernel-only coverage does not exceed three times.

                       5BSD working tree   FreeBSD baseline   Ratio
Kernel contracts               2,379             1,037         2.294x
Userland contracts               849                12        70.750x
Combined                       3,228             1,049         3.077x

Baseline: c2b7fe4a9e94a0edba9dd2772874928b565c4f9e, 2026-10-08,
FreeBSD commit '.gitignore: add tgrep index directory', author/committer
Konstantin Belousov. The baseline is an ancestor of the current source HEAD.
The complete commit metadata and current HEAD are recorded in comparison.json.
This pins the comparison to the imported FreeBSD 16 development source; it is
not a claim about every FreeBSD release or a continuously moving upstream HEAD.

How the comparison was checked
------------------------------
Run the maintained script with the same source roots, filename/directory
exclusions, macro parser and identity rules on both trees. Fetch baseline
source blobs directly from git cat-file; do not reuse the old candidate cache.
The working scan combines git-tracked candidates, visible source candidates,
and all eligible .d files, including local additions. The baseline also adds
all eligible .d files, catching multiline provider declarations. This expanded
candidate discovery reproduces the previous 1,049 baseline and includes all
year's currently retained work, not just recent instrumentation patches.

Reproduce:
  python3.12 /usr/src/tools/test/system-tracing/static-census.py \
    --out /usr/obj/5bsd-dtrace-census-recheck \
    --baseline c2b7fe4a9e94a0edba9dd2772874928b565c4f9e

Artifacts in /usr/obj/5bsd-dtrace-nineteenth-validation/census:
  working-tree.json and vanilla-freebsd.json: every identity, source path,
    recognized declaration form, provider counts and invocation-site inventory.
  comparison.json: pinned metadata, counts, ratios, additions and removals.
  working-source-hashes.json: SHA256 of exact candidate source bytes.

A contract is a distinct kind/provider/module/function/name tuple, normalizing
double underscores to DTrace's visible hyphens. Multiple call sites and copies
of the same contract do not multiply its count. Explicit SDT definitions,
inline DTRACE/ZFS_BSD forms, supported MAC/MIB wrapper definitions, ABI-neutral
linuxulator definitions, and USDT .d provider declarations are recognized.
Comments and preprocessor definition text are separated before extraction;
supported constant macro-body probes are handled explicitly. Both inventories
report zero unresolved identities among the recognized forms.

The set difference is 2,180 5BSD-only contracts and one upstream-only contract:
1,049 + 2,180 - 1 = 3,228. This round added 13 contracts and removed the previous
5BSD pts:::alloc-external contract, so 3,216 + 13 - 1 = 3,228. Source invocation
sites are a separate metric, not the basis for the 3.077x result.

Limits on certainty
-------------------
This is a reproducible static inventory under explicit parsing rules, not a
preprocessor/build-independent proof of every possible DTrace probe. It spans
architectures and conditional configurations and may include dormant source
contracts. Userland declarations are not proof that every corresponding program
was built, installed or loaded, nor that every contract has a firing path.
Test/example/doc directories and foreign /os/linux/ implementations are excluded;
see the script and comparison.json for the exact roots and exclusion names.
Generated/dynamic providers (FBT, syscall, pid, profile, etc.) are outside this
metric. ABI variants are collapsed where specified by the parser.

A runtime comparison would require matched architecture/kernel options, built
and loaded modules, matching installed binaries/processes, and dtrace -l on
both systems. /dev/dtrace is unavailable here. Therefore do not describe these
figures as '3x all runtime probes' or '3x kernel probes'. The defensible statement
is '3.077x the unique static source contracts of the pinned FreeBSD baseline,
combining kernel and userland; 2.294x for kernel contracts alone.'
